claims:
1. A method comprising:
receiving, by one or more processors, a user selection of a file containing visual content to be presented to members of a video conference by a presenter, wherein the visual content includes pages that are to be sequentially presented to the members during the video conference;
facilitating, by the one or more processors, presentation of the visual content to the members of the video conference;
obtaining, by the one or more processors, metadata associated with the visual content presented during the video conference;
receiving, by the one or more processors, customer relationship management (CRM) data from a remote system, wherein the CRM data relates to at least one participant of the video conference;
determining, by the one or more processors, feedback about the visual content by analyzing the metadata and the CRM data; and
providing, by the one or more processors, the feedback to an editor of the visual content.

